@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s47a-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-s47-deduction`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 47(b)-(d), the deduction. Row IL-08.
-- Expected values worked by hand from lines 1778-1789 and the 2026 figures (2,268; 116,400; 164,400;
-- 165,228, the same as in ito-il08-tests-s45a-s47.l4); none edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 47(b)-(d)`

`the 2026 amounts` MEANS `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year` WITH
    `the amount in section 45A(d)(1)`                                    IS 2268
    `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income` IS 116400
    `the amount in paragraph (2) of the definition of qualifying income` IS 164400
    `the average wage in the economy, in total for the tax year`         IS 165228

`no sums for section 45A` MEANS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

-- s 47 sums, positionally:   (b) fund only, (b) State or body, (b1) for the member, (b1) for a child
GIVEN `the year`     IS A NUMBER
      `work`         IS A NUMBER
      `other`        IS A NUMBER
      `insured`      IS A NUMBER
      `deposits`     IS A NUMBER
      `under (b)`    IS A NUMBER
      `under (b1)`   IS A NUMBER
      `regulations`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`in` `the year` `: work income` `work` `, other income` `other` `, insured income` `insured` `, deposits for him` `deposits` `; paid under (b)` `under (b)` `, under (b1)` `under (b1)` `; within a class of (d):` `regulations` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS `the year`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS TRUE
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS `work`
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS `other`
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS `other`
        `insured income`                                                                IS `insured`
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS `deposits`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS `no sums for section 45A`
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 47` OF `under (b)`, 0, `under (b1)`, 0
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS 0
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS 0
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS FALSE
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS `regulations`
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS FALSE

§§ `(b) — not a beneficiary member`

-- Self-employed on 100,000 (no work income), paying 10,000 to a pension fund: not a beneficiary
-- member (10,000 < 26,436.48). Limb (1): 7% of 100,000 = 7,000; 10,000 is not above 12% (12,000).
-- Limb (2): no work income, nil. Deduction 7,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; paid under (b)` 10000 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 7000
-- Paying 14,000: 2,000 above 12%, all within the further 4% (4,000): 9,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 14000 `; paid under (b)` 14000 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 9000
-- Paying 20,000: 8,000 above 12%, capped at 4,000: 11,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; paid under (b)` 20000 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000
-- An employee on 100,000 whose employer pays nothing for him (no insured income), paying 6,000 himself.
-- Limb (1) nil; limb (2) lower of 5% x 100,000 and 5% x 100,000: 5,000. Deduction 5,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 100000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 6000 `; paid under (b)` 6000 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 5000
-- An employee whose 120,000 salary is all insured income: both limbs nil, deduction nil.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `; paid under (b)` 7200 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
-- A beneficiary member has no deduction under (b): E15, 33,300 deposited, 10,800 under (b).
#ASSERT `s 47(b) — the deduction, for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 180000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 180000 `, deposits for him` 33300 `; paid under (b)` 10800 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0

§§ `(b1) — a beneficiary member`

-- Self-employed on 100,000, 30,000 paid for himself (a beneficiary member). (1): 11% of the income
-- for a self-employed member (100,000) = 11,000. (2): additional income nil. Deduction 11,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 30000 `; paid under (b)` 0 `, under (b1)` 30000 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000
-- Self-employed on 250,000, 60,000 paid for himself. (1): 11% of 116,400 = 12,804. (2): additional
-- income 116,400; the sums (2) can reach: of 47,196 not deducted under (1), what lies above 26,436.48
-- of the 60,000, 33,563.52. Both readings of the 12% test (on 47,196 or on 33,563.52) exceed 13,968,
-- so the limit is 8,148 + 4,656 = 12,804 either way. Deduction 12,804 + 12,804 = 25,608.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 250000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 60000 `; paid under (b)` 0 `, under (b1)` 60000 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 25608
-- With 40,000 paid: the sums (2) can reach are 13,563.52, below 12% of 116,400 (13,968); the 27,196
-- not deducted under (1) are above it. The two readings give 8,148 and 12,804 (fork F30): declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 250000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 40000 `; paid under (b)` 0 `, under (b1)` 40000 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 47(b1)(2) does not say whether its 12% test counts the sums its proviso excludes"
#ASSERT `s 47(b1)(1) — the deduction, for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 250000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 40000 `; paid under (b)` 0 `, under (b1)` 40000 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 12804

§§ `(d), and the tax years`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2026 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; paid under (b)` 10000 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "the regulations under section 47(d) are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`in` 2023 `: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; paid under (b)` 10000 `, under (b1)` 0 `; within a class of (d):` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `The order of the deduction and the section 45A credit (fork F35; version 0.4.0)`

-- The tests above give no sums for s 45A, so no credit competes for the payments and every reading
-- of the order gives the same deduction; they are left on the default. Here the same payments are
-- given to both sections, as a return claiming both would give them.
-- Sums for s 45A, positionally: life, pension, State, survivors, child life, child pension, not from work.
GIVEN `work`      IS A NUMBER
      `other`     IS A NUMBER
      `insured`   IS A NUMBER
      `deposits`  IS A NUMBER
      `pension`   IS A NUMBER
      `survivors` IS A NUMBER
      `under (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `under (b1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`T in 2026: work income` `work` `, other income` `other` `, insured income` `insured` `, deposits for him` `deposits` `; for s 45A pension` `pension` `and survivors' insurance` `survivors` `; for s 47 under (b)` `under (b)` `and (b1)` `under (b1)` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS 2026
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS TRUE
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS `work`
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS `other`
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS `other`
        `insured income`                                                                IS `insured`
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS `deposits`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, `pension`, 0, `survivors`, 0, 0, 0
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 47` OF `under (b)`, 0, `under (b1)`, 0
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS 0
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS 0
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS FALSE
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS FALSE

-- A self-employed individual, not a beneficiary member, 100,000 of income, paying to a pension fund.
GIVEN `paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` `paid` MEANS
    `T in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` `paid` `; for s 45A pension` `paid` `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` `paid` `and (b1)` 0

-- The independent pass's D190: 10,000 paid. Deduction first: 7% of 100,000 = 7,000 (10,000 is not
-- above 12%). Credit first: s 45A(d)(2)(b)(1) credits 5% of 100,000 = 5,000 (above the 2,268 floor),
-- leaving 5,000 for the deduction. The orders differ: declined by default, by the old name and by
-- the default's own name; each reading by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 10000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 10000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `declined where the order changes the answer` BECAUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 10000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 10000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 10000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` (`the order the taxpayer chooses` OF TRUE) EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 10000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` (`the order the taxpayer chooses` OF FALSE) EQUALS 5000
-- D236: 5,000 paid: deduction first 5,000; credit first the credit takes all 5,000, deduction 0.
-- 7,000 paid: deduction first 7,000; credit first 5,000 credited, deduction 2,000. Declined by default.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 5000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 5000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 5000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 7000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 7000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 7000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"
-- 20,000 paid: deduction first 7,000 + the further 4,000 (8,000 above 12%, capped) = 11,000. Credit
-- first: 5,000 credited, 15,000 left, the same limits: 11,000. The same: answered by default.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 20000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 20000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` EQUALS 11000
-- 12,000 paid: 7,000 first; credit first 5,000 credited, 7,000 left, 7,000. The same: 7,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`S, self-employed on 100,000, paying` 12000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 7000
-- 10,000 to the fund and 2,000 for survivors' insurance: deduction first 7,000, whatever s 45A does.
-- Credit first, the limit (5,000) cuts sums of two kinds, and which it credits s 45A does not say
-- (fork F1): so whether the order matters cannot be told, and the default declines in those words.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `and survivors' insurance` 2000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000 `and (b1)` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `and survivors' insurance` 2000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000 `and (b1)` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "section 45A does not say which sums are credited when its limits cut sums of different kinds"
-- An employee whose 120,000 salary is all insured, paying 7,200: s 47 allows nothing, so the order
-- cannot matter: 0 by default.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `; for s 45A pension` 7200 `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 7200 `and (b1)` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
-- Row IL-07's N6: 120,000 of salary of which 72,000 is insured, 16,200 deposited for him, 7,200 paid
-- by him. Deduction first: s 47(b)(2), the lower of 5% x (116,400 - 72,000) = 2,220 and 5% x
-- (120,000 - 72,000) = 2,400: 2,220. Credit first: s 45A(d) credits all 7,200 (7% of 116,400 is
-- 8,148), leaving nothing: 0. Declined by default.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 72000 `, deposits for him` 16200 `; for s 45A pension` 7200 `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 7200 `and (b1)` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` EQUALS 2220
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 72000 `, deposits for him` 16200 `; for s 45A pension` 7200 `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 7200 `and (b1)` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 72000 `, deposits for him` 16200 `; for s 45A pension` 7200 `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 7200 `and (b1)` 0) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"
-- A beneficiary member, self-employed on 100,000, 30,000 paid under (b1): deduction first 11% of
-- 100,000 = 11,000 under (1), nothing under (2). Credit first: s 45A(e)(2)(b)(1) credits 5% of
-- 100,000 = 5,000, leaving 25,000: 11,000. The same: 11,000 by default.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 30000 `; for s 45A pension` 30000 `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 0 `and (b1)` 30000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 for` (`T in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 30000 `; for s 45A pension` 30000 `and survivors' insurance` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 0 `and (b1)` 30000) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` EQUALS 11000
-- The switch names the default.
#ASSERT `section 47 — the reading this row takes of the order between the deduction and the section 45A credit` EQUALS `declined where the order changes the answer`
